# Code owners for EmergentMatter/actions
#
# This repo is pinned by every Python repo in the org, and its workflows run
# inside those repos with write access. Changes here are changes to everyone's
# CI, so they are owned rather than open.
#
# Owners can merge without a separate approval; everyone else needs one of them
# to approve. See .github/RELEASING.md for the `v1` tag rules, which are the
# other half of this: owning the files matters little if anyone can move the
# tag that decides which version of them runs.

# Everything, by default.
*                       @telafifi @evanmj @ecarrig

# The parts that execute in other people's repositories.
/.github/workflows/     @telafifi @evanmj @ecarrig
/scripts/               @telafifi @evanmj @ecarrig

# What consuming repos copy in at onboarding time. A change here does not
# reach repos already onboarded, so it is easy to under-estimate.
/templates/             @telafifi @evanmj @ecarrig

# The behavioural contract every consuming repo depends on.
/CONTRACT.md            @telafifi @evanmj @ecarrig
